    2. Randomly place blocker cells (colors 2-9) covering 40-55% of grid; scatter uniformly then lightly cluster via random walks
    3. Ensure each of colors 2-9 appears at least 5 times
    4. Remaining cells are black; verify black cells form >=2 disconnected 4-connected components (reject or re-scatter if not)
    5. Pick one large black connected component as the reachable region; remaining black components become unreached (>=1 must exist with total >=4 cells)
    6. Within the reachable region, place 5-17 blue seeds (mostly isolated, scattered); each seed replaces a black cell
    7. The input is: blockers + blue seeds + all black cells (reachable + unreached)
    8. The output is: blockers + blue seeds + reachable-region black cells turned blue + unreached black cells remain black
